                <pb facs="0316" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg218"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Holmes to Dr.
                            Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Westfield, Union County, N. J.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1900-10-18"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                18, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: I, T. D. Holmes, was with my family
                    about seven years in the interior of China. Last July we were hopelessly
                    surrounded by a Chinese mob and were about to be murdered. But Major Siao, the
                    military official of the city Kinhwa, in <pb facs="0317" n="219" xml:id="pg219"
                    /> Chekiang Province, where we were, rescued us at the risk of his own life and
                    gave us a private bodyguard and escort of twenty soldiers to Shanghai, and lent
                    us $100 besides. For this act of kindness I learn that he has been recalled to
                    Hangchao and degraded. Can not our Government look into the matter, and through
                    our ministers protest to the viceroy at Hangchao against such treatment? The man
                    had been in that position for eighteen years and was a good official.</p>
                <p>I beg that this matter may be looked into, for if he had not helped us two
                    families (eight persons) would have been murdered.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas D.
                    Holmes.</hi></signed><lb/>(Class 1890, U. of M.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
